{"4700830": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Project Phoenix 涅槃计划", "steam_appid": 4700830, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "dlc": [4873180], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>World</strong><br>In 2025, an unidentified object crashes in downtown Phoenix. The biotech giant Cerlen Group, in collaboration with the military, recovers its &quot;Core.&quot;<br>From the Core samples, Cerlen discovers an unknown virus. During research, they accidentally find it can repair severe tissue damage—at the cost of taking over the host's lower nerve centers. &quot;Project Phoenix&quot; is launched: ultimate bioweapon and medical revolution.<br>In 2028, an &quot;accident&quot; occurs at the main suburban lab. The virus mixes genetically with rabies and influenza, forming the N‑Plague—transmissible through air, blood, and water. The first infected die within 48 hours, then &quot;revive&quot; driven by the virus—losing higher cognition, retaining only the instinct to devour biomass to repair themselves.<br>Three months later, human society is paralyzed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You</strong><br>You are one of the rare &quot;Adapters&quot; with natural immunity to N‑Plague. Your blood can suppress viral spread—making you a target for survivors, Cerlen remnants, and scattered military factions.<br>You are not a hero. You are just someone who wants to live.<br>But the ruins give you no choice. Every step you take pieces together a larger truth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Exploration</strong><br>A highly open world awaits, with interactive objects offering maximum freedom.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Web‑Style Storytelling</strong><br>No fixed quest order. No mandatory NPC dialogues. No &quot;you're going the wrong way&quot; hints.<br>You can head to any location at any time—as long as you can find the way, carry enough supplies, and stay alive.<br>In each place, you pick up items, examine the environment, and connect clues.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survival &amp; Choices</strong><br>To survive the apocalypse, you must manage limited resources:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Food &amp; Water</strong> – Hunger and thirst will weaken you.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Ammunition &amp; Weapons</strong> – Every bullet counts.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Protective Gear</strong> – High‑contamination zones require hazmat suits; otherwise health drains continuously.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fuel &amp; Vehicles</strong> – Travel on foot across the wasteland, or drive trucks to haul supplies.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Enemies</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Infected (Zombies)</strong> – Slow but numerous.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Cerlen Armed Mercenaries</strong> – Well‑equipped, with one clear goal: recover all &quot;Adapters.&quot;</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Military Scraps</strong> – Remaining defensive lines that fire on any intruder.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Alien &quot;Monsters&quot;</strong> – Arriving through wormholes.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>UFO &quot;Scanners&quot;</strong> – Search for the Core, kill all living beings that enter.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>UFO Mothership</strong> …</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4700830/extras/e12455d0744929f3ec78a3b7b5dddb88.poster.avif?t=1787985018\" width=1170 height=654 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4700830/extras/e12455d0744929f3ec78a3b7b5dddb88.webm?t=1787985018\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.co